  "note": "Independent re-judgment after 562bc0139d against RFC 4271 Section 4.4 (KEEPALIVE messages MUST NOT be sent more frequently than one per second). writeMessageHeld's new step applies to *message.Notification only; a KEEPALIVE passes unchanged. publishNegotiation still raises a negotiated hold of 1-2 s to 3 s and replaces a configured keepalive at or above the negotiated hold with hold/3; the configured keepalive is whole seconds (reactor/config.go), so no configured interval is sub-second. The tests are unchanged: the positive pins the first and the periodic fire at exactly 1 s with zero jitter at hold 3; the negative checks that hold 3, 30 and 90 fire at hold/3 and never inside the first second, and that hold 0 sends none. The one-shot KEEPALIVEs on OPEN receipt and on BFD strict-mode release (session_bfd_strict.go) are one per transition. Limit of the proof: the tests drive the fsm timer, not publishNegotiation's clamp; a hold of 1 or 2 from the peer is refused before negotiation by the RFC4271-4.2-1 validator negative, not by these tests.",
